WEBVTT

00:12.480 --> 00:13.560
I wonder who that is?

00:18.920 --> 00:20.480
Is it Michiru?

00:24.810 --> 00:27.380
That's great... You're aware now aren't you, Miona.

00:27.760 --> 00:30.130
Uhm... I...

00:30.130 --> 00:31.960
Mama, it's me.

00:31.960 --> 00:34.490
I'm able to go alone to kindergarten.

00:35.950 --> 00:38.310
Uhm...Who are you?

02:39.880 --> 02:41.050
Something happened?

02:41.050 --> 02:41.870
Huh?

02:42.610 --> 02:43.550
Why do you ask?

02:43.550 --> 02:44.410
Breakfast...

02:44.850 --> 02:47.230
it was the first time where you had only one bowl.

02:48.610 --> 02:50.100
So just cheer up.

02:50.390 --> 02:51.600
Thank you.

02:53.030 --> 02:54.060
I'm all right.

02:54.540 --> 02:55.190
I see.

02:56.860 --> 02:58.240
It's hot!

02:58.240 --> 02:59.510
So hot!

03:00.720 --> 03:01.930
So much sweat...

03:02.990 --> 03:05.620
Even I have my weak points.

03:05.620 --> 03:07.660
But you're still quite arrogant.

03:09.790 --> 03:12.670
This afternoon there's a self-study break right?

03:12.670 --> 03:13.390
Yeah.

03:14.360 --> 03:16.380
Not happy about the break?

03:16.380 --> 03:17.630
Not really.

03:18.550 --> 03:19.340
You know,

03:20.450 --> 03:21.700
Asagi, today do you-

03:22.360 --> 03:23.770
Ah could you hold on for a second?

03:25.440 --> 03:26.750
Hello, this is Asagi.

03:27.460 --> 03:28.110
Yes.

03:28.710 --> 03:29.400
Oh!

03:29.760 --> 03:30.710
It's there?

03:31.180 --> 03:31.840
Okay.

03:33.260 --> 03:35.350
Ah no, I'll decide when I've seen it.

03:35.700 --> 03:36.360
Yeah.

03:37.120 --> 03:40.240
This afternoon is fine, I can go after noon.

03:40.770 --> 03:41.740
Yeah.

03:46.790 --> 03:47.760
Morning.

03:49.020 --> 03:49.660
Yo.

03:49.660 --> 03:50.980
Have you seen Sora-chan?

03:52.620 --> 03:53.830
Yeah, we came together.

03:53.830 --> 03:54.700
Together?

03:54.700 --> 03:57.980
Ah, I meant, I met her earlier at the station.

03:57.980 --> 04:01.230
It's not like you came together.

04:02.550 --> 04:03.300
I see.

04:03.300 --> 04:05.890
Ah! This afternoon, there is no lecture.

04:05.890 --> 04:07.880
I want to go out with everyone somewhere.

04:08.280 --> 04:09.260
You can't do that?

04:09.260 --> 04:10.970
Do you want to come, Midori-kun?

04:10.970 --> 04:12.560
Huh, me?

04:12.560 --> 04:13.640
No thanks.

04:13.640 --> 04:14.310
Huh?

04:14.310 --> 04:15.270
Why not?

04:15.270 --> 04:19.100
You ask why not... it's because I'm not comfortable.

04:19.520 --> 04:23.110
But it's more fun in a crowd.

04:23.110 --> 04:25.570
Ah no, no thanks really.

04:26.210 --> 04:27.120
I see.

04:27.840 --> 04:28.620
Sorry bout that.

04:28.620 --> 04:32.960
Ah, it's no problem, but if we go again on another day...

04:34.870 --> 04:39.540
As everyone knows, after the Yokohama treaty,

04:39.540 --> 04:48.470
the current system was established, with laws both protecting the liberties and regulating the magical labor of those with power.

04:48.950 --> 04:53.890
In terms of history, our lives are intertwined with our magical ability,

04:53.890 --> 04:56.650
human rights and society...

04:56.650 --> 04:58.400
Sora-chan did well.

04:58.840 --> 05:02.360
But... why didn't her memories return?

05:02.360 --> 05:03.410
Well, that's because...

05:04.450 --> 05:06.820
My magic isn't good then.

05:06.820 --> 05:08.570
That's where you're wrong.

05:08.570 --> 05:11.240
Kondo-san's request was revival magic.

05:11.240 --> 05:13.410
Besides, you completed what you had to do.

05:13.410 --> 05:18.780
But... Miona-san forgetting about Isao-san and Shion-kun, that shouldn't have happened!

05:19.210 --> 05:20.210
Sora-chan...

05:20.210 --> 05:21.670
It's not good at all!

05:22.710 --> 05:24.210
Without memories...

05:24.650 --> 05:29.550
all that were painful, all that were happy, they've all vanished.

05:30.330 --> 05:31.870
That is so sad...

05:32.490 --> 05:33.260
I...

05:33.730 --> 05:34.770
I...

05:34.770 --> 05:35.750
Sora-chan!

05:38.020 --> 05:41.100
I'm sorry, but I...

05:41.550 --> 05:42.900
Magic...

05:42.900 --> 05:46.860
regardless of how skilled you are, it isn't a perfect thing.

05:47.520 --> 05:48.930
There are things that cannot be done.

05:49.680 --> 05:54.970
Because of our forebearers, our lives as mages are guaranteed.

05:55.820 --> 05:57.990
There are things it can't do.

06:01.720 --> 06:04.160
So continue working hard on your training.

06:09.530 --> 06:10.390
Midorikawa-kun.

06:11.580 --> 06:12.750
Yes.

06:13.100 --> 06:15.430
You gave it your best on that practical.

06:15.430 --> 06:16.350
Yeah.

06:16.350 --> 06:20.020
Although it seems you still can't use magic.

06:20.020 --> 06:20.960
Yeah.

06:21.480 --> 06:25.140
But, like I said, your magic will come if you think and feel it.

06:26.370 --> 06:30.750
Magic is just like riding a bicycle, once you've done it, everything is fine.

06:31.410 --> 06:32.180
Okay.

06:32.720 --> 06:38.170
Then later, if you go out on your bicycle and go around Japan; or go out and shop,

06:38.550 --> 06:40.350
it's still the same.

06:40.760 --> 06:42.960
Okay, I think I understand.

06:43.430 --> 06:46.500
Heh, you'll be fine.

06:48.130 --> 06:48.970
You'll be fine.

06:48.970 --> 06:49.920
You'll be fine.

06:53.710 --> 06:55.100
You'll be fine.

06:55.100 --> 06:56.680
Then shall we go to Shimokitazawa?

06:56.680 --> 06:57.520
Huh?

06:57.520 --> 07:00.940
I have my eyes set on a pair of shoes that are there.

07:00.940 --> 07:03.860
I see, isn't that great.

07:03.860 --> 07:04.400
Yeah.

07:04.400 --> 07:05.940
I also want to go to Shimokitazawa!

07:05.940 --> 07:06.650
Huh?

07:06.650 --> 07:07.780
Hiyono-chan too?

07:07.780 --> 07:08.530
Yeah.

07:08.530 --> 07:12.250
Then let's all meet up at Shimokitazawa.

07:13.450 --> 07:14.210
See you later.

07:20.120 --> 07:22.470
The signal is green, what are you doing?

07:23.830 --> 07:27.210
Hiyo-chan and Hono-chan are coming to Shimokitazawa to play.

07:27.210 --> 07:30.920
Yeah, I heard the conversation from Yamabuki.

07:30.920 --> 07:33.580
What do I do if they want to go to the office.

07:34.590 --> 07:37.000
It won't be a problem, I'll just be in my room.

07:37.830 --> 07:38.510
Okay.

07:39.310 --> 07:43.690
It's kind of sad though, not being able to see Suzuki's smile.

07:43.690 --> 07:44.350
Huh?

07:46.750 --> 07:47.690
Wait up.

07:53.060 --> 07:54.040
Delicious!

07:54.580 --> 07:55.410
Isn't it?

07:55.410 --> 07:57.580
This is said to be 'THE' Shimokitazawa cafe.

07:57.580 --> 08:00.200
Although it feels like a coffee shop, its atmosphere is more like a tea house.

08:00.200 --> 08:02.710
Wow, seems like Hono-chan knows a lot.

08:02.710 --> 08:05.090
Not "seems"... but rather "does".

08:06.470 --> 08:11.170
Then, let's all head over to Sora-chan's place after we finish here.

08:12.050 --> 08:13.010
Okay...

08:13.010 --> 08:15.500
You don't seem too excited about that.

08:17.100 --> 08:18.520
Suspicious.

08:26.460 --> 08:28.350
Okay, it's moving.

08:34.390 --> 08:37.020
Ah... my magic...

08:38.650 --> 08:40.740
My heart is pounding...

08:40.740 --> 08:43.140
My heart is pounding too...

08:43.610 --> 08:46.180
Doki doki joumondoki

08:43.610 --> 08:46.180
Doki = heart beating;  joumondoki = similar to basket weaving. A bad pun.

08:50.150 --> 08:51.120
You're funny!

08:53.780 --> 08:56.090
Huh, who is that little girl?

08:56.500 --> 08:58.510
Hmm, I don't know.

08:58.510 --> 09:00.050
It's the first time I've seen her.

09:01.110 --> 09:03.020
She seems like a doll.

09:03.430 --> 09:04.610
I wonder what she's doing?

09:07.590 --> 09:09.260
Is there something you want?

09:10.170 --> 09:12.030
Oneechan, do you live here?

09:12.030 --> 09:13.530
Yes, I do.

09:13.530 --> 09:16.530
Then this place is a magic office right?

09:16.530 --> 09:21.580
Yes it is, but if you don't have a magic request, we can't help you.

09:20.970 --> 09:21.980
I...

09:22.930 --> 09:24.950
want a baby.

09:24.950 --> 09:26.380
WHAT?

09:29.500 --> 09:31.230
You want a baby?

09:32.310 --> 09:34.960
Isn't that something you should ask your mother and father for?

09:36.000 --> 09:36.900
Mother...

09:37.710 --> 09:38.660
isn't around anymore.

09:39.500 --> 09:41.530
Your mother passed away?

09:42.040 --> 09:44.680
But I have a new mama.

09:44.680 --> 09:46.060
Step mother?

09:46.060 --> 09:48.400
But if dad dies too...

09:49.680 --> 09:53.360
I will have to clean and do the laundry.

09:53.360 --> 09:55.410
Isn't that just child abuse?

09:56.290 --> 09:59.280
My new mama is scary.

09:59.280 --> 10:00.680
So sad.

10:02.050 --> 10:04.410
Are there any other adults at home?

10:05.120 --> 10:06.550
Like your grandmother.

10:07.830 --> 10:11.170
My new mama came with a new older sister...

10:11.170 --> 10:14.130
but she really is very cold towards me.

10:14.130 --> 10:16.680
Your stepmother has a mean stepsister?

10:17.650 --> 10:19.130
Do you want to tell me about it?

10:22.470 --> 10:25.440
I am Suzuki Sora, and you are?

10:26.830 --> 10:28.280
Nishihara Ruriko.

10:28.730 --> 10:31.780
Ruriko-chan, why do you wish for a baby?

10:39.350 --> 10:42.720
I want a baby, that's why I'm asking for a mage!

10:43.290 --> 10:45.080
We are mages.

10:47.070 --> 10:47.950
But...

10:47.950 --> 10:49.140
the brooms?

10:49.140 --> 10:53.880
No need for brooms, but I and these girls, all three of us are mages.

11:04.410 --> 11:07.060
Then please, a baby!

11:07.060 --> 11:11.360
Hmph, I have yet to hear of magic producing a baby.

11:11.750 --> 11:13.440
Ruriko-chan, why-

11:13.440 --> 11:15.270
Then, I'll take one from a nursery.

11:15.270 --> 11:19.110
Oh yeah, we have a delicious cake, would you like some?

11:32.350 --> 11:33.460
What should we do?

11:33.460 --> 11:35.170
She ran away fast.

11:35.170 --> 11:36.750
Geez, a baby snatcher...

11:36.750 --> 11:38.340
We should split up and search.

11:38.340 --> 11:40.010
Why do we have to...

11:40.010 --> 11:42.590
Because we can't leave her alone.

11:42.590 --> 11:44.540
But it's a half holiday for us isn't it?

11:44.980 --> 11:50.610
A child has many things they say that adults can't understand...

11:51.600 --> 11:52.480
Perhaps so...

11:52.480 --> 11:57.270
Suzuki Sora, will you waste your half holiday for a girl you don't know?

11:57.270 --> 11:59.480
Then, I'm begging you.

12:01.880 --> 12:06.890
Excuse me, has a little girl called Nishihara Ruriko...

12:07.480 --> 12:08.660
Huh, what?

12:09.080 --> 12:10.410
I haven't seen her.

12:11.030 --> 12:12.750
Thank you very much.

12:17.340 --> 12:18.840
Ah, so cute.

12:21.020 --> 12:24.970
Excuse me, are you here Ruriko-chan?

12:32.820 --> 12:37.610
Excuse me, has a little girl called Nishihara Ruriko...

12:39.830 --> 12:41.510
Ruri-chan.

12:50.380 --> 12:51.110
Huh?

12:52.010 --> 12:53.330
I came back to the same place.

13:03.610 --> 13:06.100
I pray that Ruriko-chan is safe.

13:10.290 --> 13:13.420
Ruriko-chan, I wonder where you went off to?

13:17.940 --> 13:18.950
Hello?

13:20.010 --> 13:21.060
I see...

13:25.610 --> 13:28.200
I wonder where Ruriko-chan went off to?

13:28.200 --> 13:29.870
Perhaps she went home?

13:31.580 --> 13:34.040
Can't be helped, let's use magic.

13:34.900 --> 13:39.000
Using magic without a request, we'll get in trouble...

13:45.240 --> 13:46.140
Sora-chan?

13:54.610 --> 13:56.770
All this on a half holiday...

13:56.770 --> 13:57.590
sorry.

14:01.940 --> 14:05.610
We learned that we can't perform magic without a request.

14:05.610 --> 14:06.400
Yeah.

14:07.750 --> 14:10.510
I've always thought about it,

14:10.970 --> 14:15.740
that maybe there are times when magic can be used even without request...

14:16.610 --> 14:18.260
Sora-chan is amazing!

14:19.150 --> 14:21.960
But that is a tough question.

14:22.520 --> 14:27.130
But, how can you decide if it is one of those times?

14:27.130 --> 14:28.010
Well that's...

14:29.510 --> 14:31.160
based off your intuition.

14:31.770 --> 14:33.790
Then what about now?

14:35.640 --> 14:38.400
We can't find Ruriko-chan...

14:40.190 --> 14:42.300
Let's use magic.

14:43.230 --> 14:46.570
But what kind of magic could find a person?

14:46.570 --> 14:50.550
If we used magic image, that could...

15:01.960 --> 15:03.080
Is there something you want?

15:03.690 --> 15:08.090
Ah no, I was thinking that the children were cute.

15:08.530 --> 15:14.180
That's right, they look like that, but they're actually quite rambunctious.

15:14.180 --> 15:18.120
Uhm, are you missing a child?

15:19.230 --> 15:20.750
I don't think we are.

15:21.540 --> 15:22.690
Midori-san!

15:22.690 --> 15:24.780
All our children are fine, right?

15:25.580 --> 15:26.980
They're all fine.

15:26.980 --> 15:28.190
What's the matter?

15:28.190 --> 15:30.240
There was a lady...

15:31.680 --> 15:32.950
she vanished.

15:36.950 --> 15:40.540
Seems like she's not from over here, how's it going over on your end?

15:41.300 --> 15:43.580
All the children here are accounted for.

15:45.110 --> 15:47.460
I wonder where Ruriko-chan went off to?

15:49.680 --> 15:50.760
Honomi-chan?

15:50.760 --> 15:52.300
Hey, Hono-chan!

15:52.300 --> 15:53.860
Ah, hold it!

16:11.070 --> 16:13.300
I'm at my limit,

16:14.270 --> 16:16.070
you are really tough.

16:16.570 --> 16:17.950
Ah, here!

16:18.980 --> 16:20.910
This was the cafe that we were at earlier.

16:22.790 --> 16:24.120
I see.

16:25.690 --> 16:27.150
Nishihara?

16:27.890 --> 16:30.830
I am Suzuki Sora, and you are?

16:32.120 --> 16:33.580
Nishihara Ruriko.

16:38.590 --> 16:39.760
We found her.

16:39.760 --> 16:40.360
Huh?

16:40.360 --> 16:41.490
Where? Where?

16:47.100 --> 16:48.140
Hello?

16:49.090 --> 16:50.430
Huh? Where?

16:51.440 --> 16:55.970
Okay, that's great, I'll be right there.

17:03.000 --> 17:06.540
Ah, no way, is that what she said?

17:06.540 --> 17:08.170
It's so embarrassing.

17:08.170 --> 17:11.550
She came back saying, "I want a baby!"

17:11.550 --> 17:14.080
Saying that to her papa and mama.

17:15.290 --> 17:16.920
Hey, Yamabuki Hiyori!

17:17.940 --> 17:21.350
If there was a baby, what would you do?

17:21.350 --> 17:22.060
Huh?

17:24.500 --> 17:27.100
I would play with it.

17:27.100 --> 17:28.560
With the baby?

17:28.560 --> 17:31.550
Yes, Ayumi-chan's house has a baby.

17:32.360 --> 17:33.320
I see.

17:33.320 --> 17:36.630
But, Ayumi-chan said "no" to me,

17:37.640 --> 17:40.220
that's why I want a baby...

17:41.070 --> 17:42.130
Ruriko...

17:42.920 --> 17:45.410
Ma'am, Ayumi-chan is...?

17:45.410 --> 17:48.710
One of Ruriko-chan's friends that she plays with.

17:48.710 --> 17:51.600
Ayumi-chan got mad...

17:52.740 --> 17:55.330
and said she hated Ruriko...

17:56.820 --> 18:00.900
In life, there are many things that you cannot do.

18:01.640 --> 18:05.680
I can understand how Ruriko-chan feels.

18:07.440 --> 18:11.610
Why did Ayumi-chan say that you couldn't play with the baby?

18:12.550 --> 18:17.010
When I played the piano, the baby started to cry.

18:17.810 --> 18:21.620
Then next time, why don't you try showing it a picture book?

18:22.350 --> 18:23.580
A picture book?

18:23.580 --> 18:24.820
Yeah.

18:25.740 --> 18:27.590
For instance a story about Cinderella?

18:34.230 --> 18:38.550
This store has paintings and its namesake mannequin out front, it's pretty cool.

18:38.550 --> 18:41.550
Yes, it's our pride and joy.

18:41.550 --> 18:45.970
This store's name is Arlequin, what do you think it means?

18:46.370 --> 18:48.020
Isn't it a Pierrot?

18:48.020 --> 18:54.450
Yes, Pierrot is what the Americans call him, in Europe, he's called Arlequin.

18:48.020 --> 18:54.450
Arlequin = Harlequin; Pierrot = Clown. A term to describe a comedian/comedy but slightly different

18:54.590 --> 18:56.610
That's why the picture is of a Clown.

18:56.610 --> 18:59.980
But because of that image I knew where Ruriko was.

19:01.660 --> 19:03.990
The hot crêpe was so delicious!

19:03.990 --> 19:05.910
Thank you for the food.

19:05.910 --> 19:08.540
Please come again.

19:08.540 --> 19:09.160
Okay!

19:09.160 --> 19:11.000
Please come again!

19:11.870 --> 19:12.890
Uhm...

19:14.410 --> 19:15.380
Uhm...

19:15.380 --> 19:17.920
Suzuki Sora-oneechan...

19:17.920 --> 19:18.840
Hmm?

19:18.840 --> 19:19.990
What is it?

19:21.760 --> 19:22.730
Can I...

19:23.170 --> 19:25.970
make up with Ayumi-chan?

19:25.970 --> 19:27.140
It'll be fine.

19:27.140 --> 19:28.140
Really?

19:28.140 --> 19:30.140
I'm a mage.

19:30.560 --> 19:31.970
Patching-up Friendship magic,

19:34.100 --> 19:35.690
that can be done.

19:41.480 --> 19:45.340
Ah, I wanted to see my shoes.

19:45.760 --> 19:46.870
I'm sorry.

19:46.870 --> 19:49.370
I'm feeling pretty satisfied that I got hair clips.

19:49.370 --> 19:51.710
It goes with the Yukata that I got.

19:51.710 --> 19:52.330
Yeah!

19:53.540 --> 19:55.180
Ah, excuse me.

19:56.990 --> 19:59.400
Ruriko-chan is an interesting girl.

19:59.810 --> 20:02.260
The three of us were tricked by her.

20:04.320 --> 20:06.800
She was so cute, Ruriko-chan.

20:06.800 --> 20:09.140
Her mother passed away...

20:09.140 --> 20:11.800
The stepmother and the mean stepsister...

20:17.480 --> 20:22.010
Today was the first time that I did anything with friends.

20:22.620 --> 20:23.740
Friends?

20:23.740 --> 20:26.810
Yeah, my first mage friends!

20:29.220 --> 20:30.450
Yamabuki Hiyori!

20:30.450 --> 20:31.040
Hmm?

20:31.040 --> 20:32.660
Come, let's go!

20:32.660 --> 20:35.080
Then Sora-chan, see you tomorrow!

20:36.560 --> 20:39.420
Sora-chan, see you tomorrow!

20:40.380 --> 20:41.880
What are you smiling about?

20:41.880 --> 20:43.100
Friends...

20:49.200 --> 20:50.100
That's your third bowl.

20:50.100 --> 20:50.840
Huh?

20:52.270 --> 20:53.140
I'm glad.

20:53.140 --> 20:53.890
Huh?

20:53.890 --> 20:54.680
What's this?

20:54.680 --> 20:55.980
A secret conversation?

20:55.980 --> 20:56.780
Idiot.

20:57.490 --> 20:59.380
Is this mabu tofu too spicy?

20:59.860 --> 21:02.860
It's not good unless it is spicy.

21:02.860 --> 21:03.840
Thank you.

21:04.990 --> 21:07.030
Sayori-chan, another bowl please.

21:07.030 --> 21:08.570
It's Sayori-obasan right!

21:11.260 --> 21:12.200
What is that sound?

21:14.960 --> 21:16.860
Don't check your mail during a meal.

21:18.190 --> 21:19.010
Gota-kun!

21:21.830 --> 21:22.950
It's from Kuroda.

21:23.930 --> 21:25.090
Kuroda?

21:25.090 --> 21:26.070
Another trainee?

21:28.620 --> 21:29.350
That guy said...

21:29.670 --> 21:30.730
he's quitting.

21:31.160 --> 21:32.140
Huh?

23:06.150 --> 23:09.370
Do people always have difficulties on the road of life?

23:10.000 --> 23:13.220
At that time, can you talk to your friends about it?

23:13.790 --> 23:15.090
Next time, Crossroads.

23:15.750 --> 23:19.580
When I'm worried, I take a nap first.
